{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take","id":1094998,"title":"Anything you have the Technocracy can take?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-20T19:54:33-07:00","id":1094998,"title":"Anything you have the Technocracy can take?","content":"The Technocracy has often been portrayed as all powerful on many occasions and I'm curious as to how true that is. Can a mage make it so the Technocracy can't just take his Node, Sanctum, job, or girlfriend even if they are aware of the mage and where to find him? <br /> <br /> This is actually less to do with Mage and more to do with Changeling. Changeling books tend to talk about the Technocracy in terms of capturing Freeholds and sanitizing them. If, after monumental effort, a band of Changelings perform Reverie and Rapture in a specific location long enough that it can be turned into a level 5 Freehold and then the Technocracy finds out, is it possible for the Changelings to simply tell the Technocracy to piss off?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T20:23:31-07:00","id":1095004,"title":"","content":"Well, that depends. The answer is technically 'no' - nothing you do can ever make you totally safe from your enemies no matter who or what they are, barring outright Ascension or removing yourself totally from existence and into a different one. In practical terms, yes, it's actually very easy to make it so they 'can't <i>just</i> take'. The <i>just</i> is the key. All you have to do is make it too risky for the Technocracy to sanction, which is easy enough to do with three key ingredients.<br /> <br /> 1. Stay discreet. The quiet Hermeticist who isn't summoning spirits to bring him his car keys and instead is easy for everyone, including other mages, to mistake as just 'guy with a good occult library and good luck', isn't going to get the same priority of purging as 'I AM LORD ALDEMORT, WIELDER OF THE SEVENTY-TWO NAMES, AND I COMMAND THEE TO BRING ME A SLURPEE FROM THE 7/11, HAZIMEL!'<br /> <br /> 2. Surround yourself by critical infrastructure or lots and lots of innocent lives, preferably 'valuable' ones. If one word from you can blow the shit out of a preschool, the more Human technocrats might have second thoughts about going after you with full force - especially if you've managed to pull off #1. If it can also shatter a piece of useful - ideally <i>Technocratic</i> and not just mundane - infrastructure, even the ones who forgot about kindness and mercy might have to rethink their strategy.<br /> <br /> 3. Always have a smokescreen and operate through it. It wasn't you at the house next to the Technocratic Warehouse and Mr. Robot's Preschool for Precocious Youngsters (ITX had to go into some weird sidelines to make the budget meet this last year, alright? Don't question it.) even if, to all casual or even moderately in depth examinations, it appeared to be you. It was a consor you'd smudged about a bit until he looked like you, had a similar aura to you, and wrapped in enough 'you' to pop positive as you for divination etcetera. Your real names (including your magical motto) should never appear linked in any way to your smokescreen.<br /> <br /> As for a bunch of changelings, well, that depends on where the Freehold is and which game is taking precedence. Are you playing Changeling? Then yes, with Heroic and Valiant effort - preferably with stirring speeches, some kind of magic quest, and a rallying cry for allies from the opposing court or even the shadow court in this Hour of Direst Need - the Changelings can win. Bonus points if the win requires the Great and Noble Sacrifice of a Hero. If it's Mage, nah, they're pretty much fucked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T00:18:35-07:00","id":1095040,"title":"","content":"I'd say Number 2 on that list is something you should only do if you have a death wish. One of the few Craftmason ideals that the Technocrats haven't purged is 'it's better to tear down a flawed house and start anew than to live in it.' You would become a flaw, in their house. The Infrastructure being important only makes it MORE of a slap in the face. It would buy you time. At best. Not even a long time.<br /> <br /> And given such valuable infrastructure would undoubtedly have surveillance, you're essentially shooting your capacity to do numbers 1 and 3, which are about keeping out of sight in the foot.<br /> <br /> In any case. I treat the Technocracy much like I treat Megacorps in shadowrun. They act only when the cost is less than the gain. If you have a rank 20 node, with only minimal defenses. You can bet that an army is going to show up at your doorstep. So in short. Don't take more than you can defend and you're fine because there are plenty of others who DO take what they can't defend.<br /> <br /> If you mean &quot;If for some bizarre reason, the technocracy decides that this particular spot needs to be purged at all costs!&quot; Then no. You're pretty much fucked. But they don't DO that unless there's a very pressing reason. Code Ragnarok has been used ONCE. And the Union has been around for centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T00:44:52-07:00","id":1095045,"title":"","content":"A key point is the Technocracy actively courts banality. While this makes them seriously bad new for Changelings it also makes it really hard for them to see most Freeholds at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T01:13:28-07:00","id":1095055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095040#post1095040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Number 2 on that list is something you should only do if you have a death wish. One of the few Craftmason ideals that the Technocrats haven't purged is 'it's better to tear down a flawed house and start anew than to live in it.' You would become a flaw, in their house. The Infrastructure being important only makes it MORE of a slap in the face. It would buy you time. At best. Not even a long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surveillance is only an issue if you either make your presence known or are entirely too obvious. Or if you literally live right on top of it, which is not what I said - you live near, not in, the 'too much collateral' target. You live where paradox will almost certainly bite them just as hard as it'll bite you, or where any kind of fighting is going to wreck their shit as well as your's, and while they might be furious when they discover you, they can't act immediately.<br /> <br /> Which dovetails into this. If the Technocracy wants to pound you down, you're going down no matter what - unless you're, say, Voormas or Senex. The best you can do is make it not worth their effort to do so as soon as they discover you exist, and to make it so that - if they do decide to move on you, which they inevitably will - their options are limited. That way you have both time and options to relocate, set up a killing field, or fake your own death. It's much easier to deal with one assassin than an entire assault force, and a lot easier to run when you have to if the 'time to go!' isn't a full-scale attack with HIT Marks and armoured suits and voidship support.<br /> <br /> Be the guy in a busy part of Chicago who they have to handle with some subtlety, not the guy at Greylocke Chantry they can blow to pieces with a mech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T02:29:40-07:00","id":1095069,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the key here it's to be sure that putting you down isn't worth the effort.<br /> <br /> You're not fighting against a single enemy, but against an overaching organization that encompases more than the planet earth. What you're asking it's like &quot;can my freehold survive a fight with the Garou Nation&quot;...well, if the garou believe you're a treath on the level of the Storm Eater, then no, there's no way you can survive against them...but if you're not that treathening, then you're not fighting against the Garou Nation, but against a pack or two. Sure, they can ask for reinforces, but what are the odds that they will receive them?...if you're too hard to take, and not too much of a treath for the Nation as a whole, they may decide to allow you to stay rather than face the humillation of asking other Garou (and, likely, be refused).<br /> <br /> With the Technocracy you can play a similar strategy. The Technocracy it's more prone to send reinforces than the Garou Nation, but it has too many fronts to take care off. If they consider that you aren't worth the effort, they will leave you for the end of their &quot;to do&quot; list. And, since it's a very long list, this may buy you a couple of centuries.<br /> <br /> To do this you need to be powerful enough so it's a pain in the ass to take you down, harmelss enough so it's not so much of a pain in the ass to live with you, and worthless enough so puting you down doesn't compensate the effort.<br /> <br /> You can't beat the Technocracy, but the local Amalgam?, yes you may be able to beat the local Amalgam. If you're too much to take in an elegant move, they might need to ask for reinforcements...but if they do, they need to provide evidence that you're worth the effort to move troops and money to take. If they just ask for help because they would like to keep your freehold, and it isn't big enough to make a difference for the local projects of the Technocracy, while you're not very treathening to people nor to the Consensus, then the Symposium might decide that the Amalgam isn't very efficient (even if they decide to send the reinforces)...and no Amalgam wants that.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, this it's what Archmages do. 9/10 if the time, the Technocracy preffers to let them rot in their Horizon Realms rather that send a fleet to take them down...then again, that's more or less how Porthos met his fate, so even being at THAT power level isn't a total guarantee-though OoH had that chantry in Mars during 500 years (more or less) without being too subtle about it, so you can say that having overwhelming power and being useless does buy you some time. <hr /><br /> It's worth to note than to detect a Freehold you need Spirit in addition to Prime (as per Lost Dreams), so only a Construct with a Void Engineer can truly discover your little powersource. Heck, only a Void Engineer, or a guy with dots in the very rare Dimensional Science may have the power to see the true natrue of your faes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-21-2017, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T03:37:35-07:00","id":1095077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take#post1094998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy has often been portrayed as all powerful on many occasions and I'm curious as to how true that is. Can a mage make it so the Technocracy can't just take his Node, Sanctum, job, or girlfriend even if they are aware of the mage and where to find him?<br /> <br /> This is actually less to do with Mage and more to do with Changeling. Changeling books tend to talk about the Technocracy in terms of capturing Freeholds and sanitizing them. If, after monumental effort, a band of Changelings perform Reverie and Rapture in a specific location long enough that it can be turned into a level 5 Freehold and then the Technocracy finds out, is it possible for the Changelings to simply tell the Technocracy to piss off?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Technocracy can do almost anything but it has limits on its influence due to fighting the entire WOD simultaneously. If they discover your freehold, they WILL return but it may be a year or ten years later because they have other problems.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:00:08-07:00","id":1095174,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if you're running your own campaign it's better to make the technocracy weaker than it appears to be in the earlier editions. M20 has more balance and less 'bad history' in this aspect as well as a 'use what you want the way you want' attitude that allows for a wider diversity in story telling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:05:46-07:00","id":1095199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095055#post1095055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Surveillance is only an issue if you either make your presence known or are entirely too obvious. Or if you literally live right on top of it, which is not what I said - you live near, not in, the 'too much collateral' target. You live where paradox will almost certainly bite them just as hard as it'll bite you, or where any kind of fighting is going to wreck their shit as well as your's, and while they might be furious when they discover you, they can't act immediately.<br /> <br /> Which dovetails into this. If the Technocracy wants to pound you down, you're going down no matter what - unless you're, say, Voormas or Senex. The best you can do is make it not worth their effort to do so as soon as they discover you exist, and to make it so that - if they do decide to move on you, which they inevitably will - their options are limited. That way you have both time and options to relocate, set up a killing field, or fake your own death. It's much easier to deal with one assassin than an entire assault force, and a lot easier to run when you have to if the 'time to go!' isn't a full-scale attack with HIT Marks and armoured suits and voidship support.<br /> <br /> Be the guy in a busy part of Chicago who they have to handle with some subtlety, not the guy at Greylocke Chantry they can blow to pieces with a mech.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have ways of hiding any level of force they choose to use. It's entirely possible for them to, if they want to, drop an assault force in the middle of downtown manhattan at the busiest time of day and NOONE will know that it's happening. Hiding in a city is a TERRIBLE idea.<br /> <br /> It strongly depends on WHERE you are. And given correspondence makes for easy travel to anywhere on earth. There is no reason WHATSOEVER for you to have your sanctuary anywhere near a Technocrat stronghold, which pretty much rules out most of Europe, Japan, and the USA, Maybe Russia.<br /> <br /> Yes. If you set up a chantry of wizards in the middle of New York. They're going to just murder you. But why would you do that? That's stupid. So instead you set up in the Solomons Islands. Or the Middle East. Or Africa. China. Some of the more impoverished areas of Eastern Europe. South America. Anyplace where the Technocrats don't have a death grip. Then when you need to go to Seattle? You use your teleporter closet. You set up safehouses. Disposable apartments and things with portals to your chantry that can be abandoned at will.<br /> <br /> As the Taftani demonstrated, outside of their home turf, the Technocracy CAN be fought to a standstill.<br /> <br /> Go someplace where a strike against you will start a war. And they'll probably leave you alone until they're ready to start a war. Which given the way they operate, could be decades. Centuries even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T17:26:16-07:00","id":1095301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095199#post1095199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They have ways of hiding any level of force they choose to use. It's entirely possible for them to, if they want to, drop an assault force in the middle of downtown manhattan at the busiest time of day and NOONE will know that it's happening. Hiding in a city is a TERRIBLE idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hiding in a city gives you a far larger population base to blend in with. Do you have an example of them sending a full scale assault force, void ships and all, into Downtown Manhattan in 'the busiest time of day' (or an analogous situation)? How many resources did they have to expend to do it just to keep paradox off their backs?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It strongly depends on WHERE you are. And given correspondence makes for easy travel to anywhere on earth. There is no reason WHATSOEVER for you to have your sanctuary anywhere near a Technocrat stronghold, which pretty much rules out most of Europe, Japan, and the USA, Maybe Russia. </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, for cultural reasons, available nodes that have been overlooked, and the need to continue fighting the good fight against the Technocracy. Oh, and that whole 'hide where they least suspect you' thing. I take it you also have a very low opinion of pretty much every published mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. If you set up a chantry of wizards in the middle of New York. They're going to just murder you. But why would you do that? That's stupid. So instead you set up in the Solomons Islands. Or the Middle East. Or Africa. China. Some of the more impoverished areas of Eastern Europe. South America. Anyplace where the Technocrats don't have a death grip. Then when you need to go to Seattle? You use your teleporter closet. You set up safehouses. Disposable apartments and things with portals to your chantry that can be abandoned at will. </div> </div> </div>Of course, first they have to find your chantry exists. Then they have to pinpoint it. And then they have to actually have the resources available to assault it on hand before you can rabbit. And as you just so generously pointed out, correspondence makes for easy travel anywhere, so it doesn't really matter where you go, now does it? They can just boop into existence right on top of you if they find out you exist, so it really makes very little difference whether you're in New York City or in Taihiti save for the degree of enemy presence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As the Taftani demonstrated, outside of their home turf, the Technocracy CAN be fought to a standstill. </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, the Middle East, where the Technocracy definitely didn't totally dominate the paradigm for decades and wreak cultural and environmental devastation. Great job those Taftani did!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Go someplace where a strike against you will start a war. And they'll probably leave you alone until they're ready to start a war. Which given the way they operate, could be decades. Centuries even. </div> </div> </div>If they can drop a totally hidden full-sized assault force on you in the middle of Manhattan's rush hour, in public, and have no one at all know what happened? There is <i>nowhere</i> on Earth you can hide where 'a strike against you will start a war', for the simple reason they apparently have the ability to use full force perfectly unseen anywhere they like. Either they are the undisputed masters of Stealthy Blitzkrieg or they aren't. Which is it?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T18:16:09-07:00","id":1095310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095301#post1095301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hiding in a city gives you a far larger population base to blend in with. Do you have an example of them sending a full scale assault force, void ships and all, into Downtown Manhattan in 'the busiest time of day' (or an analogous situation)? How many resources did they have to expend to do it just to keep paradox off their backs?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except, of course, for cultural reasons, available nodes that have been overlooked, and the need to continue fighting the good fight against the Technocracy. Oh, and that whole 'hide where they least suspect you' thing. I take it you also have a very low opinion of pretty much every published mage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, first they have to find your chantry exists. Then they have to pinpoint it. And then they have to actually have the resources available to assault it on hand before you can rabbit. And as you just so generously pointed out, correspondence makes for easy travel anywhere, so it doesn't really matter where you go, now does it? They can just boop into existence right on top of you if they find out you exist, so it really makes very little difference whether you're in New York City or in Taihiti save for the degree of enemy presence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ah yes, the Middle East, where the Technocracy definitely didn't totally dominate the aradigm for decades and wreak cultural and environmental devastation. Great job those Taftani did!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If they can drop a totally hidden full-sized assault force on you in the middle of Manhattan's rush hour, in public, and have no one at all know what happened? There is <i>nowhere</i> on Earth you can hide where 'a strike against you will start a war', for the simple reason they apparently have the ability to use full force perfectly unseen anywhere they like. Either they are the undisputed masters of Stealthy Blitzkrieg or they aren't. Which is it?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A Population you as an awakened mage stick out from like a sore thumb to anyone using watch the weaving, or the technocratic alternative thereof. A fairly basic power. Might I add. Your best bet isn't in blending in with the sleepers, because you can't. Your best bet is being off the map where they aren't actively able to look for to strike at you. And yes, they have a piece of gear that's basically a police line. Anything past the line is hidden from sleepers and looks utterly normal. From there you just get trucks to go in and THEN the cyborg kill squad levels the place. Oh no. A terrorist attack. Darn those Taftani. You have a few hours while they put together the team and then set up the barricades.<br /> <br /> Cultural reasons are irrelevant to strategic reasons. And yes. I find the established characters rather silly. But that's part of the way games are run.<br /> <br /> Let me just find the giant quintessence spewing hole in reality. Totally difficult guys. And no. They have to have scanned your location prior. They can't just use a sympathetic link to YOU. what do you think this is? Magic? So being someplace in the third world where they can't look for you as easily, because the mages there are predominantly opposed to them, is essential. The war you'd start is not between sleepers. Which is your audience for your suggested 'hiding in plain sight.' but your fellow mages.<br /> <br /> And no. The Technocracy didn't dominate the Paradigm for Decades. The Taftani have ruled the roost in the middle east since prior to desert storm and continue to do so up into the present day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T18:31:05-07:00","id":1095316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095310#post1095310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Population you as an awakened mage stick out from like a sore thumb to anyone using watch the weaving, or the technocratic alternative thereof. A fairly basic power. Might I add.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fairly basic power that is far from universally used on every population centre. If it was, there would be no Traditionalists or disparates or orphans roaming around the Western world unmolested. But there are - and a great many of them. There are also ways to obscure your presence from those powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your best bet isn't in blending in with the sleepers, because you can't. Your best bet is being off the map where they aren't actively able to look for to strike at you. </div> </div> </div>In the middle of a population center, you in fact can blend in because your house is just one more house. Your car is just one more car. When you order incense, you're just one more person getting some funky smells going on among a teeming population where thousands of people do that daily. The ebb and flow of quintessence around you and your home could be residue from a thousand other sources. If you're in an isolated compound, however, the Technocracy can and will find you anyway - just ask Greylocke - and anything you have sticks out like a sore thumb. Got a house on a mountain, alone? That'll show up on a satellite feed. Got a power line to it? That'll show up too, and good luck stealing the neighbour's juice if he's twenty miles away. (And while, yes, a mage has no great need for electricity if they can just use magic, using magic for everything is a much better way to attract attention than 'I own a fridge and a phone'.)<br /> <br /> [quote[And yes, they have a piece of gear that's basically a police line. Anything past the line is hidden from sleepers and looks utterly normal. From there you just get trucks to go in and THEN the cyborg kill squad levels the place. Oh no. A terrorist attack. Darn those Taftani. You have a few hours while they put together the team and then set up the barricades.[/quote]<br /> <br /> I asked you if there is a single example of them doing so, and I would like you to directly answer that question. Is there? Where? And while we're at it, where's this piece of gear from, and what are its downsides? Why don't we see it employed on the regular?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cultural reasons are irrelevant to strategic reasons. And yes. I find the established characters rather silly. But that's part of the way games are run. </div> </div> </div>Mage is a game of cultural clashes and the pursuit of world views and ideologies. Cultural reasons <i>are</i> the strategic reasons, or no one would give a fuck what anyone else was doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me just find the giant quintessence spewing hole in reality. Totally difficult guys. And no. They have to have scanned your location prior.They can't just use a sympathetic link to YOU. what do you think this is? Magic? So being someplace in the third world where they can't look for you as easily, because the mages there are predominantly opposed to them, is essential. The war you'd start is not between sleepers. Which is your audience for your suggested 'hiding in plain sight.' but your fellow mages. </div> </div> </div>If they can simply use a sympathetic link to you - which means <i>you fucked up</i> in the first place - then where you are makes essentially zero difference. If they don't have one, they do need to have established your location prior, yes - and that is why you take efforts to hide that location by obscuring the source of quintessence, hiding obvious signs of magick, and setting up front.<br /> <br /> Also, they are already at war with those other mages, so why exactly should they care about 'starting a war' with them? Sleepers are in fact much more dangerous to the Technocracy when it engages in large-scale operations than other mages are, because other mages can be fought on even footing. Sleepers, while powerless, get to kill you just by being a witness to you doing anything out of the paradigm. <i>Sleepers</i> are your best security, not other mages you have no cultural, ethnic, social, or religious ties to and who may in fact view you as a dangerous rival, a threat, or an unwanted invader - since your hypothetical stance is 'hey let's just leave new york and go live in the middle of the Sudan/Borneo/Taihiti/Wherever'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no. The Technocracy didn't dominate the Paradigm for Decades. The Taftani have ruled the roost in the middle east since prior to desert storm and continue to do so up into the present day. </div> </div> </div>[Citation Needed], since a big deal with the ahl-i-Batini leaving the Council was that it opened up the Middle East to Technocratic control.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T18:52:28-07:00","id":1095322,"title":"","content":"They aren't looking EVERYWHERE at once. They're looking at certain places at once. It's like whack a mole. If you're careful you slip away. If you're not you get whacked. Building a fort right next to the hammer chain is not being careful.<br /> <br /> If you live in the western world, you're bombarded by surveillance from all sides. You leave a data trail everywhere. and the Technocracy is looking for you in it. If you LEAVE the western world, the surveillance gets much lighter. Sure a satellite can spot your hideout in the slums of some city in India. But the surveillance is nowhere near as intense. So your chances of getting spotted are much much smaller.<br /> <br /> That is the example. Them using that piece of gear to cover up a void ship crashing in the middle of town during rush hour. Just a car accident folks. Move along. It's disadvantage is that you have to actually keep people physically out. Not hard to do with the manpower offered by the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> And no. They AREN'T at war with them. The Pogrom is over. The Union acts to stamp out those who are threats to their power but they aren't actively starting wars nine times out of ten.<br /> <br /> Also, the Batini left the council in the VICTORIAN era. I said prior to Desert Storm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T19:05:02-07:00","id":1095323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095322#post1095322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't looking EVERYWHERE at once. They're looking at certain places at once. It's like whack a mole. If you're careful you slip away. If you're not you get whacked. Building a fort right next to the hammer chain is not being careful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are looking at certain places. So you avoid being seen in those places, and exploit the blindspots. You don't go to Mr. Robot's Preschool for Precocious Children, but you maintain a presence just close enough that a strike will risk damaging it and where they wouldn't expect a Traditionalist presence - where the Magic Eyes aren't looking. Add some basic precautions to conceal your presence from brief scrutiny and you should be just fine for the short to medium term that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you live in the western world, you're bombarded by surveillance from all sides. You leave a data trail everywhere. and the Technocracy is looking for you in it. If you LEAVE the western world, the surveillance gets much lighter. Sure a satellite can spot your hideout in the slums of some city in India. But the surveillance is nowhere near as intense. So your chances of getting spotted are much much smaller. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you also leave behind your family, your friends, your culture, and your entire way of life. I mean, sure, <i>you can </i>run and hide, but that's essentially surrendering. It's also, as we all know, utterly impossible for any Traditionalist mage to avoid the data trail, turn it to their advantage, or subvert surveillance with a variety of magical tools and techniques including but not limited to 'make friends with a Virtual Adept'. Did you forget that the Technocracy are far from the undisputed masters of the digital arena?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is the example. Them using that piece of gear to cover up a void ship crashing in the middle of town during rush hour. Just a car accident folks. Move along. It's disadvantage is that you have to actually keep people physically out. Not hard to do with the manpower offered by the Technocracy. </div> </div> </div>What book is that from, and since when was 'a ship crashed' equivalent to 'we just sent in the Magic Army to blow shit up'?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no. They AREN'T at war with them. The Pogrom is over. The Union acts to stamp out those who are threats to their power but they aren't actively starting wars nine times out of ten. </div> </div> </div>Then you can live anywhere in safety so long as you lay low. Except of course that your entire premise is that you can't do that, so clearly, the war is cold - but not <i>over</i>. If it was over, you could happily set up shop in the middle of New York City.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the Batini left the council in the VICTORIAN era. I said prior to Desert Storm. </div> </div> </div>I think you will find that in the course of human history, the Victorian era predates Desert Storm. Perhaps you might be so good as to nominate what particular decades you meant?<br /> <br /> Please stop trying to dance around the questions. If you continue, I won't. I honestly don't have time for someone trying to avoid giving direct answers at the moment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T19:18:14-07:00","id":1095326,"title":"","content":"As an additional side note, having checked my timeline file the Ahl-i-Batini did not leave the Council until after the Victorian era had been over by 21 years. The Technocracy enjoyed dominance in the Middle East from around 1904 (at the earliest, and the 1920s at the latest) until 1979 marked the start of their forced withdrawal, so I'd say that fairly constitutes 'decades' of control, wouldn't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T19:27:48-07:00","id":1095329,"title":"","content":"Mages can mask their presence among the billion magical occurrences that the Technocracy regularly does not regulate. Like random spiritual activity, vampires and ghouls, sorcerers, bursts of resonance due powerful emotions, urban legends coming true...etc.<br /> <br /> In the old NWO Convention book they talk about the kind of radars that Technocracy uses to detect magic, and how they only have personel to control the most egregious uses of magic...because the cities are so full of reality deviance (which it's not the same as reality deviants) that they just can't go everywhere each time a blip appears in the radar. Thus it doesn't seem they can do this, or at least not without a kind of effort they usually don't make.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">they have a piece of gear that's basically a police line. Anything past the line is hidden from sleepers and looks utterly normal. From there you just get trucks to go in and THEN the cyborg kill squad levels the place. Oh no. A terrorist attack. Darn those Taftani. You have a few hours while they put together the team and then set up the barricades.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, they can do this, but the fact that they need to deploy that line it's already asking for a Device that basically screams: &quot;I can't take care of this deviants without blowing the city block&quot;...which in turns means the Syndicate AND the NWO may not be very happy unless you can demonstrate that the treath it's worth leaving all elegance and discretion and use vulgar magick (carefully controled under the tape).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let me just find the giant quintessence spewing hole in reality. Totally difficult guys. And no. They have to have scanned your location prior. They can't just use a sympathetic link to YOU. what do you think this is? Magic? So being someplace in the third world where they can't look for you as easily, because the mages there are predominantly opposed to them, is essential. The war you'd start is not between sleepers. Which is your audience for your suggested 'hiding in plain sight.' but your fellow mages. </div> </div> </div>Erm...you know the third world has cities too...don't you? Of course, I agree that in US you're pretty much in Technocracy turf, while in other countries the Traditions have a bigger hold...you're obviously better in a place that follows your Paradigm, with a lot of Traditionalist Chantries ready to back you if any metal-head enters the place. That's a given.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And no. The Technocracy didn't dominate the Paradigm for Decades. The Taftani have ruled the roost in the middle east since prior to desert storm and continue to do so up into the present day. </div> </div> </div>Nope, the ones that have dominated middle east paradigm for centuries are the islamic mages of the Ahl I Batin, but they do so in the cities, and for centuries they have had to keep a low profile because of the Technocracy taking the Nodes of the Web of Faith, among other internal issues. The fire sorcerers of the Taftani, that seem like they had come from the 1001 nights, dominate an empty desert (the Empty Quadrant) that has very little value to the whole of the Technocracy...and part of their strategy as far as I'm aware consisted in having genies located in hidden places among cities. if the Technocracy tries to enter in their worthless desert, they can blow half middle east merely by releasing them. The Technocracy can contain this treath, but this would mean calling Void Engineers to earth to search for hidden spirits, while they should be taking care of...other important matters...outside reality.<br /> The *success* of the Taftani it's merely due their lack of importance (who wants that desert anyways). On the other hand, the much more powerful ans sucessful Ahl I Batin (who recently founded their own &quot;Traditions&quot;), have been there in the shadows for centuries, in the cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-21-2017, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T19:40:25-07:00","id":1095333,"title":"","content":"Sure, the Technocracy has surveillance everywhere in the developed world. But all that data is useless if they don't know what to look for. And Traditionalists do not register their identities and magickal affiliations with some central Mage authority. They pop up everyone - Awaken anywhere - and get recruited by whoever happens to find them first. By default, the Technocracy does not know about the existence of any given individual Tradition or Craft mage. Not unless they are given reason to know that a particular person - in an enormous sea of people - is one of their ideological opponents. <i>Only then</i> will they have reason to look through the mountains of surveillance data, let alone find anything in it.<br /> <br /> This is why laying low and being discreet can allow a Tradition or Craft mage to operate in the middle of a major metropolitan area, while escaping the Technocracy's eyes. Walking around town wearing wizard robes makes the stand out, so the mage doesn't wear them outside their Sanctum, save in circumstances where they <i>need</i> to draw upon the Mythic Threads far afield.<br /> <br /> Except &quot;wearing robes attracts attention&quot; <i>isn't actually necessarily true</i> either. Weirder crap goes on in New York subways and streets all the time. Ren fairs and fan conventions further populate the land with people dressing up in elaborate costume. After a while of this, the Technocracy has learned to tune out &quot;false positives&quot; in their surveillance data. They have to, or they'd spend an unacceptable amount of time and resources chasing dead ends. Indeed, this is how the Traditionalists make predominantly Technocratic areas amenable to Traditionalist presence: by invading their sober, serious reality with a dose of casual madness, that is perpetuated by Sleepers.<br /> <br /> On the flipside, Traditionalists have not been idle for the centuries they fought the Technocracy. They build wards to mask the presence their Nodes. They erect &quot;Ignore Me!&quot; fields around their homes and on their persons, so people don't notice them. They use simple Forces rotes (or Bafflejacks, as detailed in M20) to disrupt electronic surveillance. They use Entropy on their credit cards, so their financial transactions get harder to trace. You don't even need to be a technomancer, like the Virtual Adepts or Society of Ether, to interact with the technological world. Mystics, despite their reputation as regressive and unchanging, have been adapting their methods to modern problems. Most mystic Traditions have a faction devoted to blending their arts with tech, for exactly this purpose.<br /> <br /> And mages spread these rotes around, operating a brisk trade of tricks to dodge the Technocracy. If only to have more product to trade with, it spurns on further rote development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 05-21-2017, 10:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T23:42:03-07:00","id":1095387,"title":"","content":"It needs to be remembered that the Pogrom is not in effect anymore. Or maybe &quot;not in effect again yet&quot;, who knows.<br /> Either way, the Technocracy currently isn't on a &quot;kill or process all Traditionalists&quot; trip, and more on an &quot;Observe, calculate threat level, Reality Deviance and statistical probability for paradox. Subvert or assault if they become an actual projected Problem&quot;<br /> <br /> Magus McMagick practicing their craft in private and meeting in their circle of deviants isn't going to have much of a problem from the Technocracy. They will be observed if noticed, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> However, if they begin to try and influence sleepers in a public manner, the Technocracy will pull some levers to counteract that - mostly subtle levers. Deals falling through, required permits being really strict, sponsors for events jumping ship...such things.<br /> Also plain out threatening the Mage's relatives wellbeing, or putting the Mage under threat of losing their home and job ( Or even better, threatening to make the relatives lose their home and job.. ) can do *wonders* if the Mage's character is realistically fleshed out and still has a mundane life.<br /> Let's not kid ourselves. Even if you suddenly can do magic something has to pay the bills, you still love your normal friends, your family, like the home you have, and nobody wants to apruptly lose the mundane life they still can manage. Most people'd not be near the 'lol okay I use my spheres to make something new' kind of shallow.<br /> <br /> Only if the Traditionalist and their fellow ilk become an actual threat that can't be contained through more mundane means and influence do they send in the heavy hitters.<br /> <br /> It's more cost effective, too.<br /> And the Technocracy works much better in most stories as an ever-present oppressive element, than ActionMen In Suits that you need to fistycuff on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-22-2017, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T00:00:32-07:00","id":1095392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095329#post1095329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On the other hand, the much more powerful ans sucessful Ahl I Batin (who recently founded their own &quot;Traditions&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can I read about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T00:20:44-07:00","id":1095394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095392#post1095392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can I read about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's called the &quot;Disparate Alliance&quot;. M20 made it an entire fifth side in the Ascension War, and staffed it will all most notable Crafts. It was a whole thing.<br /> <br /> Have we not been over this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T00:41:22-07:00","id":1095399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095394#post1095394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's called the &quot;Disparate Alliance&quot;. M20 made it an entire fifth side in the Ascension War, and staffed it will all most notable Crafts. It was a whole thing.<br /> <br /> Have we not been over this?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I read &quot;their own Traditions&quot;, I imagined something new like eight (or nine if you include an Entropy-wielding group) Arabic and Batini themed Crafts mirroring the Council of Nine Mystic Traditions; it would be a sixth major group of Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-22-2017, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T03:30:15-07:00","id":1095423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1094998-anything-you-have-the-technocracy-can-take?p=1095399#post1095399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I read &quot;their own Traditions&quot;, I imagined something new like eight (or nine if you include an Entropy-wielding group) Arabic and Batini themed Crafts mirroring the Council of Nine Mystic Traditions; it would be a sixth major group of Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Traditions have never been unified in ideology. So if the Batini made their own, just strictly looking at that earlier model, it would not be all-Arabic/Middle Eastern mages. It would be what the Disparate Alliance is: a loosely allied group of vastly different magical groups from all over the world, and who have a lot of work to do in order to remain a united force, despite half of them hating all the others vehemently.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't think the Batini have a strong enough ethos on their own to justify any Crafts being made from them. They have enough material for exactly one group: the Ahl-I-Batin. The Taftani and various Choristers make up the remaining bulk of the mystical material from the region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T05:24:49-07:00","id":1095450,"title":"","content":"I have the view the Technocracy should also be thought of as an organization which is not actually in CONTROL but doing STEERING.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy does not control the CIA, much less the United States of America. The NWO has agents in the NSA and taps all of their information but the vast majority of NSA employees work for the NSA not the Union. <b>But </b>its members probably include the guy who advises the guy who advises the President. Not enough to Mind 4 dominate POTUS into complete obedience (and risk massive paradox backlash) but enough to do some Mind 2 sympathetic magic which will work a bit in the long run to get their agenda passed through Congress if they do one or two successes every month for years. They also use Sleeper lobbyists and cash like everyone else.<br /> <br /> The Syndicate has wires in Wallstreet so they can &quot;Foci&quot; causing the crash of stock or raising of it but it doesn't own maybe more than 1 to 3 Fortune Five Hundred companies. It <i>invests</i> in the other 497 (as well as launders its magically generated money through them) but Pentex is the group which actually bothers running day-to-day company policy for its possessions. The NWO has the ability to call the cops and have your license changed so you're a registered sex offender and wanted for murder as well as rape. It has better things to do than actually <b>employ</b> cops, though. The Syndicate can electronically alter your bank records and have funds transferred to theirs. However, the banks are almost inevitably run by Sleepers. Hell, the group more likely to control your local cops, news network, and bank is the Camarilla versus the Technocracy. The Technocracy is global while the Camarilla is feudal.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is a (comparatively) tiny cabal of mages at the heart of Western civilization with a few thousand operatives as well as researchers for each Convention. It just APPEARS huge because it <i>hides</i> in the WOD's genuinely massive secular capitalist 21st century society. The Men in Black aren't just their agents but also the FBI, SIS, Interpol, and NSA and anyone else who actually does the grunt work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3cur1uMGrxs\" data-code=\"3cur1uMGrxs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3cur1uMGrxs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> The Technocracy would also rather let 100 mages get away than risk someone discovering them. While it's good copy to send a bunch of Hit Marks to slaughter a bunch of fairies on paper, the simple fact is that those Hit Marks have to come back to a Construct somewhere. If that gets found out, then that Construct is compromised as well and will get an endless number of Marauders after it.<br /> <br /> As such, for my Technocracy, they prefer to go soft if they can (try to buy the land, intimidate the fae into leaving, or yes stir up trouble with Dauntain) before launching D-Day. They have enough trouble with the Traditions, Nephandi, and Marauders before borrowing it from a bunch of reality deviants playing LARPs (even if they do have a node worth capturing). A game against the Technocracy would be built better about why the cops suddenly believe the place is full of drugs and endangered children with the goal of finding the ONE Technocracy agent involved and shutting him down.<br /> <br /> I call this the &quot;1st Edition Mage where combat isn't the focus&quot; portrayal.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it's still a bad idea to **** with them but they're a threat best thought in terms of influence rather than rulership. Even they sometimes forget it and their belief helps shape reality--it's just there's maybe 10,000 of them and 7 billion of us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-22-2017, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}